--- body ---
## Context

0037 defines the design: `erg validate` becomes per-file format + ref-existence
only; `erg check` handles full-corpus DAG coherence, ID uniqueness, and folder
closure. This ticket implements both commands in the binary.

## Actions

### A. `erg validate <files…>`

Change `cmdValidate` to:
- Require explicit file arguments (no directory default; print usage if none given)
- Check per file: magic line, header syntax, required fields, log format (existing)
- Check per file: each `Blocked-by:` local ref exists as a filename in the same
  ticket dir (glob `{dir}/{id}-*.erg`); forge refs skipped as offline-unknown
- Never recurse into subdirectories
- Exit 0 if all pass, 1 on any error

### B. `erg check [dir]`

New command:
- Default dir: `tickets/`
- Load all `.erg` files recursively from dir
- Check: no duplicate IDs across all files
- Check: no cycles in the Blocked-by graph (DFS)
- Check: all local Blocked-by refs resolve to a known ID
- Check (warn only): open tickets in `closed/` subdir or vice versa
- Output: `PASS` or per-violation lines `VIOLATION <file> <code>: <desc>`
- Exit 0 if no errors (warnings do not fail)

### C. Tests

- `test_validate.sh`: update to pass explicit file args; add test for
  "no args → usage error"
- New `test_check.sh`: cycle detection, duplicate ID, cross-folder warn

## Exit criteria

- `erg validate <files>` accepts only file args; no directory scanning
- `erg validate` (no args) prints usage and exits non-zero
- `erg check [dir]` detects cycles, duplicate IDs, unresolved local refs
- Folder closure mismatch emits a warning (exit 0)
- All existing tests pass; new tests cover the above
